  {
   "id": "y6QnDajmW7EJ",
   "from": "Ian Pylvainen",
   "author": "346f36192106cd17",
   "date": "2014-06-02T20:02:57Z",
   "subject": "Re: getting error while plotting a graph",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi Dharmendra,<div><br></div><div>This is actually an RStudio issue (rather than a Shiny issue) and I encourage you to post it over on our RStudio open-source support forum at <a href=\"https://support.rstudio.com/hc/communities/public/topics\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://support.rstudio.com/hc/communities/public/topics&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792402573977000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2vk58UuLWLGHYPwKOHtdIb\">https://support.rstudio.com/hc/communities/public/topics</a> for the best possible support.</div>\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>That being said, typically this is an error that R is unable to contact the png device from within RStudio - you should check and see if the same commands work within R itself rather than RStudio. If they don&#39;t, its likely an issue with how you&#39;ve compiled R and you need to make sure you&#39;ve compiled it with png support.</div>\r\n\r\n<div><br></div><div>You can also try running the following commands:</div><div><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">sessionInfo()</span><br style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">capabilities()</span><br style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">png(); dev.off()</span><br style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">x11()</span><br style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px\">Sys.getenv(&quot;DISPLAY&quot;)</span><br style=\"font-family:arial,sans-serif;font-size:13px\"></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">in both RStudio and R and let us know on the support forums what your results are - that will help us troubleshoot what&#39;s going on here.</font></div>\r\n\r\n<div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Thanks,</font></div><div><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Ian</font></div>\r\n</div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
